From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 20:44:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] mtld3d: readbacks staged and PageBox pages from the unix side
 under the winemetal facade
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

MacNeutron's Direct3D 9 on winemetal (D3D9 spec §5.1): in the VM's guest
a Metal buffer is made only over memory winemetal handed out, so under
the facade a readback goes through a staging buffer copied out once
complete, and the PE side takes its PageBox pages from two new unix
calls (AllocPages, FreePages) when GetDeviceInfo sets PAGES_FROM_UNIX;
the loopback build serves them with anonymous mappings, the VM build
with winemetal's guest allocator.

Assisted-by: Claude Code: claude-opus-5-5
